course: dictionary
lesson: 1659
title: Sound words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a sound for your ears. Chirrup means to make a series of short, high sounds, like a bird or an insect. When you read «The Rat chirrups, and up climbs the Otter», you can picture small, bright noises by the river.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Who or what chirrups? Birds, insects and sometimes people. In this sentence the Rat makes the sound, and the Otter climbs up next, so chirrup is a sound a creature makes. Test it: put "chirp" in its place and the sentence still makes sense, so chirrup means something very close to chirp.
explain: Chirrup can also be a noun, a chirrup. A person can chirrup too: «chirruped happily» tells you the voice was bright, cheerful and high. So this word shows feelings as well as sounds.
fact: Chirrup means to make a series of short, high sounds, like a bird or an insect; it is much like chirp.
fact: «Sparrows chirrup» and «crickets chirrup on summer nights».
fact: A person can chirrup too, when they talk in a bright, cheerful, high voice.
fact: Chirrup is also a noun: a chirrup is one such sound.
fact: The verb forms are chirrup, chirrups, chirruped and chirruping.
exercise: «In summer, the crickets chirrup all night long.» What does chirrup mean here? | To swim fast across a river | To fall down slowly | *To make short, high sounds like an insect | To shout very loudly at the sea
exercise: «The Rat chirrups, and up climbs the Otter.» What does «chirruped happily» tell you about a character? | *Their voice sounded bright and cheerful | They were cold and tired | They were climbing a tall tree | They were fast asleep
exercise: Find and copy the noun that means one short, high sound. | came | hedge | from | *chirrup
test: The word chirrup is a verb. Which form shows that something happened in the past? | chirruping | *chirruped | chirrup | chirrups
test: In «The Rat chirrups, and up climbs the Otter, shaking himself and grumbling «Greedy beggars!»», what is the Otter doing? | Chirruping to the birds | Sleeping by the river | Singing a song | *Climbing up the bank
exam: Which sentence uses chirrup as a noun? | We chirruped with delight. | The crickets are chirruping now. | The sparrows chirrup at dawn. | *The sparrow's chirrup woke me at dawn.
